    {
      "id": "19055",
      "key": "SFCC-650",
      "summary": "pdp/add-to-bag",
      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1. Given a shopper lands on a PDP and no size has been selected, when the page loads, then the Add to Bag CTA is displayed but disabled."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2. Given a shopper attempts to click Add to Bag without selecting a size, when the click is registered, then the button remains inactive and a \"Size required\" inline message is displayed."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3. Given a shopper selects an in-stock size, when the selection is registered, then the Add to Bag CTA becomes active and enabled."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "4. Given a shopper clicks Add to Bag with a valid size selected, when the action is triggered, then the cart API call is made and the button displays a loading state while the call is in flight."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "5. Given the cart API call completes successfully, when the response is received, then the item is confirmed as added to bag and the appropriate success state is shown."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6. Given the cart API call fails, when the error response is received, then an inline error message is displayed and the CTA returns to its enabled state so the shopper can retry."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "7. Given a product is a one-size item, when the component is rendered, then the size is treated as pre-selected and the Add to Bag CTA is active on page load."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "8. The component accepts size selection state and stock status as props — it does not manage size selection itself; that is owned by pdp/size-selector ("
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCard",
                  "attrs": {
                    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-648#icft=SFCC-648"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ")."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "9. Given a keyboard user tabs to the Add to Bag CTA, when the component receives focus, then a visible focus ring is displayed per the design system spec."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "10. Given the CTA is in a disabled state, when a screen reader user reaches it, then it is announced as unavailable so the user understands action is required before proceeding."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "11. Given an inline error or success message is displayed, when it is triggered, then the message is announced via an ARIA live region without requiring the user to navigate to it."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "12. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA as the minimum accessibility standard."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "19051",
      "key": "SFCC-648",
      "summary": "pdp/size-selector",
      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1. Given the component is rendered with a list of sizes, when no size has been selected, then the selector displays in its default state with a placeholder label."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2. Given a shopper selects a size, when the selection is confirmed, then the selector displays in its filled state showing the selected size."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3. Given the selector is in focus/open, when the size list is displayed, then it renders in its active state showing all size options."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "4. Given a size is passed a stock status of in stock, when rendered, then it displays as a standard selectable option."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "5. Given a size is passed a stock status of low stock, then it displays with a low availability indicator per design spec (PRD-012)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "6. Given a size is passed a stock status of out of stock, then it renders as a non-selectable, visually disabled option (PRD-014)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "7. Given a size is passed a stock status of notify me, then it renders with a Notify Me label per design spec (PRD-016); the Notify Me interaction itself is handled by a separate story."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "8. Given a size is passed a status of recommended, then it displays with a recommended indicator per design spec."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "9. Given no valid size is selected and the selector is in an error state (triggered externally, e.g. by Add to Bag), then the error state renders per design."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "10. Given the component is rendered on mobile, then it renders using the mobile variant per the design system spec."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "11. Given the product has only one size, when the component is rendered, then the standard size selector UI is not displayed; instead a plain One size text label is rendered in its place per the approved PDP designs (PDP Low availability frame, file QQ427wHWEUjsjP7H8v48Rs)."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "12. Given the product has only one size, when the component is rendered, the size is automatically considered selected and no shopper interaction is required to enable Add to Bag."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "13. Given a keyboard user tabs to the size selector, when the component receives focus, then a visible focus ring is displayed per the design system spec."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "14. Given a keyboard user has focused the size selector, when they press Arrow Up or Arrow Down, then focus moves between size options without requiring a mouse."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "15. Given a keyboard user has focused a size option, when they press Enter or Space, then that size is selected."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "16. Given the size selector is in an error state, when the error is triggered, then focus is retained on or moved to the selector so the user is aware without needing to navigate to it."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "17. Given a screen reader user navigates to a size option that has a stock status indicator (low availability, notify me, out of stock), when the option is read out, then the stock status is included in the accessible label — e.g. \"Size 1 (US 6), Low Availability\" — so screen reader users receive the same information as sighted users."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "18. Given the selector is in an error state and an error message is displayed, when the error is triggered, then the message is announced via an ARIA live region without requiring the user to navigate to it."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "19. Given a size option is out of stock and non-selectable, when a screen reader user reaches that option, then it is announced as unavailable rather than simply being skipped or visually greyed out."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "20. Given the product has only one size and the One size label is displayed, when a screen reader user reaches it, then it is announced correctly as the selected size."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "21. The component meets WCAG 2.1 AA as the minimum accessibility standard."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "18130",
      "key": "SFCC-92",
      "summary": "PDP — Size Selection & Add to Bag",
      "customfield_10231": {
        "value": {
          "type": "doc",
          "version": 1,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1. Given a shopper opens a PDP, when the page loads, then the correct product variant and stock status data is fetched from SFCC and passed as props to pdp/size-selector ("
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCard",
                  "attrs": {
                    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-648#icft=SFCC-648",
                    "localId": "d57575e8538b"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ")."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "2. Given a shopper opens a PDP, when the page renders, then pdp/size-selector and pdp/add-to-bag are rendered in the correct position per the approved Figma designs, on both desktop and mobile."
                },
                {
                  "type": "hardBreak"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3. Given a shopper selects a size, when the selection is made, then the selected size state flows correctly to pdp/add-to-bag ("
                },
                {
                  "type": "inlineCard",
                  "attrs": {
                    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-650#icft=SFCC-650",
                    "localId": "3fd451cf1fc9"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ") and the CTA becomes active."
                }
              ],
              "attrs": {
                "localId": "3845b0a4f22c"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

