      "value": "The Definition of Done (DoD) sets the minimum criteria a user story must meet before it is marked Done and shown in the sprint review. A story that misses any criterion is not Done and moves to the next sprint, regardless of progress.\n\nThis standard applies to both squads.\n\n| Criteria | Description | Verified by |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Development complete | All coding and implementation for the feature or task is finished. | Developer / Tech Lead |\n| Peer reviewed | The code or solution has been reviewed by at least one other team member to ensure quality and adherence to standards. | Peer reviewer |\n| API Contracts Tested | All API contracts related to the development have been thoroughly tested. | Developer / QA |\n| QA tested | The feature or task has undergone Quality Assurance testing to identify and resolve defects. | QA |\n| Acceptance criteria passed | The developed solution meets all predefined acceptance criteria agreed upon by stakeholders. | Product Owner / BA |\n| No Critical defects | There are no critical bugs or issues that would prevent release or proper functioning of the feature. | QA / Tech Lead |\n| Documentation updated | All relevant documentation, including technical specs, user guides, or API docs, has been updated to reflect the changes. | Developer / Product Owner |",
      "format": "markdown"
    }
  }
}"}

