ested owners where possible. Do not create the story yet — show me the draft first.\n\nOnce the draft is approved:\n\nCreate this as a Jira story in project SFCC: - Summary: [short title] - Epic: [epic key] - Assignee: me - Functional Area (customfield\\_10236): [e.g. PDP / Home Page / PLP / Search / Integration] - Squad (customfield\\_10237): [Squad A / Squad B] - Rollout Scope (customfield\\_10242): [select all that apply: AU, AE, EU - Domestic, EU - International, HK, UK, US - Domestic, US - International] - Labels: [HPC-034;Custom;Squad-A] - Description: As a [persona], I want [goal], so that [benefit]. [any additional context] - Acceptance Criteria (customfield\\_10231): [numbered Given/When/Then statements] - Dependencies (customfield\\_10232): [@Name: open item or question] - Priority: [High / Medium / Low]\n\n### Story format\n\n**Summary** — short title only, e.g. `Footer – Join Us Email Capture & Registration Modal`. Do **not** put the \"As a / I want / so that\" here. Keep it scannable for the backlog.\n\n**Description** — the full user story sentence, followed by any additional context needed for developers or testers. The description must contain only the user story and context — never AC or dependencies:\n\nAs a [persona], I want [goal], so that [benefit]. [Any additional context]\n\n**Acceptance Criteria** — always Given/When/Then, numbered for traceability, one criterion per statement. Cover the happy path, edge cases, and negative tests where relevant. Goes in the dedicated **Acceptance Criteria field** (`customfield_10231`), not in the description.\n\n1. Given [context/precondition], when [action], then [expected outcome].\n2. Given ...\n\n**Labels** — format: `HPC-034;HPC-035;Custom;Squad-A` — semicolons, no spaces. Always include:\n\n* The Req ID(s) the story covers (from the functional requirements page)\n* `Custom` or `Config`\n* `Squad-A` or `Squad-B` (taken from the parent epic's label in Jira)\n\n**Functional Area** (`customfield_10236`) — picklist reflecting the functional area of the story. Values in use: `PDP`, `Home Page`, `PLP`, `Search`, `Integration`. Use `Integration` for stories that are primarily about connecting SFCC to an external system, regardless of which epic they sit in.\n\n**Squad** (`customfield_10237`) — set to `Squad A` or `Squad B` based on the parent epic's label in Jira.\n\n**Rollout Scope** (`customfield_10242`) — multi-select checkbox defining which storefronts this story applies to. Select all that apply:\n\n* `AU` — Australia (domestic + Oceania)\n* `AE` — Middle East (Global-e)\n* `EU - Domestic`\n* `EU - International` (Global-e)\n* `HK` — Hong Kong (Global-e)\n* `UK`\n* `US - Domestic`\n* `US - International` (Global-e)\n\nIf the story applies to all storefronts, select all. If it is storefront-specific (e.g. a Global-e-only integration story), select only the relevant ones.\n\n**Assignee** — set to yourself when creating. Claude runs under your Jira credentials so specifying \"me\" or \"assign to me\" will assign it to you automatically. Note: passing \"me\" does not resolve via the Jira API — always use the reporter's email address directly instead (the reporter field is auto-populated and can be read from the created issue).\n\n**Open Items / Dependencies** — goes in the **Dependencies field** (`customfield_10232`). Where possible, assign an owner per item. For suggested owners refer to [1.2 Team Overview](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/261586947/1.2+Team+Overview).\n\n@[Name]: [question or dependency]\n\n**Epic** — always link to the relevant epic. If unsure of the epic key, ask Claude: *\"What is the epic key for [area] in project SFCC?\"*\n\n**Priority** — High / Medium / Low\n\n### Personas\n\nAlways check [04.3 Personas](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/245694470). Common personas:\n\n| Persona | Who |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Shopper** | End customer browsing/buying |\n| **Site Merchandiser** | Business user managing products/content in BM day-to-day |\n| **Site Admin** | Technical user doing one-time platform configuration |\n| **Developer** | Used for enabler stories (e.g. sample data load) |\n\n### Splitting stories — frontend vs backend\n\nWhen a requirement involves both a UI component and backend logic (e.g. a form and its integration to an external system, or a product attribute and how it renders on a page), write **two separate stories** — one for the frontend and one for the backend. Different developers typically work on each, even within the same squad.\n\n### Bulk creation\n\nThe preferred approach is one story at a time, drafted and reviewed in the Claude chat. When you have a batch of straightforward stories to create at once, bulk creation is also supported — but always review the proposed list before confirming.\n\nCreate the following Jira stories in project SFCC, all under epic SFCC-[N], all [priority] priority, all labelled \"[label]\", assigned to me, Functional Area [value], Squad [A / B], Rollout Scope [list storefronts]: 1. [summary] 2. [summary] 3. [summary] Show me the list before creating anything so I can confirm.\n\n### Sequencing within an epic\n\nStories should be sequenced so that:\n\n1. **Foundation stories come first** — data model, attribute schema, taxonomy must exist before anything else\n2. **Enabler stories unblock downstream work** — e.g. a sample data load story should be sequenced early so other developers can build and test against real data\n3. **Integration stories come last** — built against the foundation, tested against sample data first\n4. **Flag MuleSoft/third-party dependencies explicitly** in labels and the Dependencies field\n\n### Config vs Custom\n\n| Type | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Config** | SFCC out-of-the-box — just needs configuring in Business Manager |\n| **Custom** | Requires a custom build (PWA component, custom attribute, custom logic) |\n\n### Scope boundary — Accenture vs Zimmermann\n\nAccenture scope ends at **SFCC platform + PWA Kit + SFCC-side integrations**. Flag the following in open items but do not build:\n\n* MuleSoft development\n* GTM / analytics container logic\n* Content authoring in Contentful\n* Google Merchant feed configuration\n* UAT, performance testing, pen-test execution\n* BM training and org change management\n\n### API error handling — field failures\n\nWhen creating a story via the Jira API, individual fields can fail independently. If a field fails:\n\n* **Do not fall back to putting its content in the description.** The description must only ever contain the user story and context.\n* **Do not abandon the other fields.** Set all remaining fields correctly in the same create call, then follow up with a separate update call to retry the failed field.\n* **Report the failure explicitly** — tell the user which field failed and that it needs to be set manually or will be retried.\n\nThe description, AC (`customfield_10231`), and Dependencies (`customfield_10232`) are three separate fields and must always be kept separate, even if a field update fails.\n\n#### Setting customfield\\_10231 (Acceptance Criteria) and customfield\\_10232 (Dependencies)\n\nThese fields must be passed as **plain text strings** via the `additional_fields` parameter — not via the `fields` parameter, and not as ADF (Atlassian Document Format) objects. Passing them as ADF or via `fields` will return an error.\n\n**Correct approach — use `additional_fields` with plain text strings:**\n\nDefaultnoneadditional\\_fields: {\n\"customfield\\_10231\": \"1. Given ... when ... then ...\\n2. Given ... when ... then ...\",\n\"customfield\\_10232\": \"@Name: open item or question.\\nDepends on SFCC-XX.\"\n}\n\n**Do not do this — passing as ADF object will fail:**\n\nDefaultnonefields: {\n\"customfield\\_10231\": { \"type\": \"doc\", \"version\": 1, \"content\": [...] }\n}\n\n**Do not do this — passing via `fields` as plain text will also fail:**\n\nDefaultnonefields: {\n\"customfield\\_10231\": \"1. Given ...\"\n}\n\nThis applies to both create and update calls. Always set these two fields via `additional_fields` with plain string values.\n\n### Common mistakes\n\n| Situation | Wrong | Right |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| AC format | Bullet checklist in description | Numbered Given/When/Then in `customfield_10231` |\n| AC location | AC written into the description field | AC goes only in `customfield_10231` — never in description |\n| AC API call | Passing `customfield_10231` via `fields` or as ADF | Pass via `additional_fields` as a plain text string |\n| Dependencies location | Dependencies written into the description field | Dependencies go only in `customfield_10232` — never in description |\n| Dependencies API call | Passing `customfield_10232` via `fields` or as ADF | Pass via `additional_fields` as a plain text string |\n| Open items | Free text in description | In `customfield_10232`, with owner where possible |\n| Labels | `HPC034` or `HPC-034, Custom` | `HPC-034;Custom;Squad-A` (semicolons, no spaces) |\n| Squad label | Assumed from functional area | Check the parent epic's label in Jira |\n| Functional Area | Left blank | Set `customfield_10236` — use `Integration` for external system stories |\n| Squad field | Left blank | Set `customfield_10237` to `Squad A` or `Squad B` |\n| Rollout Scope | Left blank | Set `customfield_10242` — select all applicable storefronts |\n| Assignee | Left unassigned or passing \"me\" to the API | Assign at creation time using the reporter's email address directly (\"me\" does not resolve via the Jira API) |\n| Field API failure | Dumping failed field content into description | Set all other fields correctly; retry the failed field separately; report the failure to the user |\n| Splitting stories | One story covering UI + integration | Two stories — one frontend, one backend |\n| Starting without FRs | Going straight to Jira | Check [04.1 Functional Requirements](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/301793284) first |\n\nPart 2 — Jira Backlog Management\n--------------------------------\n\n### Searching the backlog\n\nShow me all open stories in epic SFCC-[N], sorted by priority. Include assignee and status. Show me all stories in project SFCC labelled \"checkout\" that are not yet started. Show me all Jira stories assigned to me in project SFCC that are In Progress or To Do. Show me all stories in project SFCC updated in the last 7 days. Show me all stories in project SFCC with priority Blocker or Critical that are not Done.\n\n### Updating a story\n\nUpdate Jira story SFCC-[N]: - Change priority to Critical - Add label: go-live-blocker - Add this to the description under a new heading \"Additional Context\": [text]\n\nTo reassign:\n\nReassign SFCC-[N] to [name or email]. Add a comment: \"Reassigned to [name] per standup [date].\"\n\n### Transitioning status\n\nJira statuses have underlying transition IDs that vary per project. Claude checks available transitions automatically.\n\nMove SFCC-[N] to \"In Progress\". Move SFCC-[N] to \"In Review\". Add comment: \"PR raised — #[N]. Waiting on QA sign-off.\" Close SFCC-[N] as Done. Add comment: \"Verified in STAGE environment [date].\"\n\nBulk transition:\n\nMove all stories in the current sprint of project SFCC that are \"In Review\" and have label \"[label]\" to \"Done\". Show me the list before changing anything.\n\n### Adding comments\n\nAdd a comment to SFCC-[N]: \"[text]\"\n\n### Linking stories\n\nLink SFCC-[N] to SFCC-[M] as \"blocks\" — SFCC-[N] blocks SFCC-[M].\n\n### Sprint management\n\nAdd stories SFCC-[N], SFCC-[M], SFCC-[O] to the active sprint on the SFCC board. Show me all stories in the active sprint on the SFCC board. Group by status. Include story points if available.\n\nPart 3 — Cross-Cutting Patterns\n-------------------------------\n\n### After a workshop\n\nI've just come out of a discovery workshop. Here are my rough notes: [paste notes or transcript excerpt] Do two things: 1. Update Confluence page ID [N] — add today's decisions as a new dated section. 2. Create Jira stories in project SFCC for each open action item. Use epic [key], priority Medium, label \"discovery\". Show me the proposed stories before creating them.\n\n### Sprint planning from a spec\n\nHere is our sprint planning doc. Extract all items marked [STORY] and create them as Jira stories in project SFCC. Map [EPIC] tags to the corresponding epic keys. Flag anything where the epic key is ambiguous and ask me before creating. [paste doc]\n\n### Status reporting\n\nGive me a status summary for the SFCC project: - Stories completed this week (moved to Done in last 7 days) - Stories currently In Progress with their assignees - Any stories flagged as blocked or with priority Critical/Blocker - Count of stories remaining in the current sprint Format it as a brief update I can paste into a Slack channel.\n\n---\n\n*Project: Zimmermann Magento → SFCC | Accenture Song | Last updated: July 2026*",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

