      "summary": "Promotional Announcement Banner — Contentful",
      "description": "As a \nSite Merchandiser, \n\n\nI want \nthe promotional announcement banner content managed in Contentful, \n\n\nso that \nI can configure banner messages, CTAs, rotation timing, page visibility, and scheduling without requiring a developer deployment.\n\n\nThis story is a follow-up to SFCC-51 (Promotional Announcement Banner UI), which builds the PWA component with mock content. This story covers the Contentful content model and the integration between Contentful and the PWA Kit component so that the banner is fully content-managed.\nComponent should handle the following flexibility, Site Merchandiser should be able to configure:\nconfigurable per storefront\nconfigurable per customer group\nconfigurable per logged in status\nconfigurable time of rotation (set time appropriately for the length of the message for accessibility standards)\nconfigurable pages\nconfigurable position\nconfigurable message\nconfigurable CTA\nconfigurable enablement on/off\nconfigurable content - content scheduling (start/end time)",
      "status": {
        "name": "To Do",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "labels": [
        "Contentful",
        "Custom",
        "HPC-017",
        "Squad-A"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "18139",
      "key": "SFCC-94",
      "summary": "Homepage Content Row — Flexible Grid & Image Carousel",
      "description": "As a\n Site Merchandiser,\nI want\n to configure homepage image rows to display a variable number of columns (2, 3, or 4) and optionally cycle through more images than are visible at once,\nso that\n I can control the visual layout and cadence of campaign and editorial content on the homepage to suit each seasonal drop.\nContext:\nSFCC-90 establishes the homepage module structure with content rows currently built as fixed 4-column grids. This story adds two layers of flexibility to those rows, both controlled entirely via Contentful — no code changes should be required for the merchandiser to change the layout of a row.\nGrid flexibility:\n The number of visible columns per row is configurable in Contentful (2, 3, or 4). The PWA renders the appropriate column layout based on the value set on the content entry. Each column displays a CMS-managed image with its own CTA link.\nCarousel behaviour:\n If more images are added to the content entry than the configured column count, the row becomes a carousel — the additional images cycle in as the shopper navigates or the carousel auto-advances. If the number of images equals the column count, the row renders as a static grid with no carousel controls.\nExample: a 3-column row with 9 images loaded in Contentful renders as a 3-column carousel cycling through 3 sets of 3 images.\nThis component can be built against mock Contentful content before the full content model is finalised, in line with the approach established in SFCC-90.",
      "status": {
        "name": "To Do",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "labels": [
        "Custom",
        "HPC-008",
        "HPC-009",
        "Squad-B"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "18122",
      "key": "SFCC-90",
      "summary": "Homepage Layout & Content Modules UI",
      "description": "As a \nShopper, \n\n\nI want\n to land on a homepage that presents Zimmermann's seasonal campaigns, featured products, and editorial content in a structured and visually engaging layout, \n\n\nso that\n I can discover new collections, explore the brand, and navigate easily to the products and content I care about.\nThe homepage is composed of the following content modules, in sequence from top to bottom:\nFull-width hero banner\n — A full-bleed image at the top of the page with headline text and a CTA link. Supports full-bleed or padded variants per design.\nFeatured product tiles row\n — A row of 4 product tiles surfacing featured or new-arrival products, each linking to the relevant PDP.\nCampaign/editorial image links row\n — A row of images linking to edits, campaigns, or editorial landing pages.\nShop the Look hero\n — A large-format hero image with a \"Shop the Look\" module positioned to the right, allowing the shopper to explore and navigate to featured products from the look.\nTop categories row\n — A row of category tiles, each with a campaign image, linking to the relevant category PLP.\nEditorial and/or boutique duo\n — A final row containing two equal-width (for desktop) hero images side by side: one linking to an editorial destination and one linking to the boutiques page or store locator.\nThis component can be built with mock content prior to Contentful content model being finalised.",
      "status": {
        "name": "In Refinement",
        "category": "To Do",
        "color": "blue-gray"
      },
      "labels": [
        "Custom",
        "DesignDependent",
        "HPC-008",
        "HPC-009",
        "Squad-A"
      ]
    }
  ]
}"}

